usage: log show [options] <archive>
   or: log show [options]

description:
    Show the contents of the system log datastore or a log archive.
    Output contains only default level messages unless --info and/or
    --debug are specified.

options:
    --[no-]backtrace                  Control whether backtraces are shown
    --[no-]debug                      Control whether "Debug" events are shown
    --[no-]info                       Control whether "Info" events are shown
    --[no-]loss                       Control whether message loss events are shown
    --[no-]signpost                   Control whether signposts are shown
    -A, --archive <archive>           Display events stored in the given archive
    -c, --color <mode>                Control color output (valid: auto, always, none)
    -D, --directory <directory>       Display events from the given directory path
    -E, --end <date>                  Display events up to the given end date
    -l, --last <num>[s|m|h|d] | boot  Display recent events up to the given limit
    -L, --last24                      Display last 24 hours
    -Y, --yesterday                   Display the previous day
    -T, --today                       Display since the start of the day
    --[no-]pager                      Paginate output using less
    -H, --highlight-predicate <predicate>
                                      Highlight filtered events using the given predicate
    -P, --predicate <predicate>       Filter events using the given predicate
    -p, --process <pid> | <process>   Filter events using the specified process
    --metric                          Display metrics events
    --realtime                        Annotate output with "Real-Time" if the process uses the RT Logging system
    --source                          Annotate output with source file and line-number
    -S, --start <date>                Display events from the given start date
    -s, --style <style>               Output format (valid: default, syslog, json, ndjson, compact)
    -Z, --timezone local | <tz>       Use the given timezone when displaying event timestamps
    --mach-continuous-time            Print mach continuous time timestamps rather than walltime
    --unreliable                      Annotate output with whether the log was emitted unreliably

valid time formats:
    'Y-M-D H:m:s+zzzz', 'Y-M-D H:m:s', 'Y-M-D', '@unixtime'

predicate usage:
    Filter predicates follow the NSPredicate format described at:
    https://developer.apple.com/library/content/documentation/Cocoa/Conceptual/Predicates/AdditionalChapters/Introduction.html

    For predicate field/type details, see `log help predicates`.

shorthand usage: 
    Shorthand is converted to a predicate. For details, see `log help shorthand`.

